105				// append-only transcript ran ahead of the last disk export), so
106				// the file is recoverable and safe to sweep.
107			case bytes.HasPrefix(cached, data):
108				// The disk export ran ahead of the last checkpoint. Keep the
109				// file out of the sweep instead of blocking every future export;
110				// a later checkpoint reconciles it and the next sweep collects
111				// it. Checkpoint-backed exports repeat this proof so the file is
112				// never deleted while it still holds the only copy of the tail.
