132				// way (the error path deleted nothing), so refusing to sweep it
133				// loses no bytes, while the export goes on and every other session
134				// gets through. It is exactly what the newer-than-its-checkpoint
135				// case above already does, for the reason stated there -- "instead
136				// of blocking every future export".
